--- result.json ---
{
  "avg_fps": 137.3,
  "low_1pct_fps": 45.4,
  "cause": "PCIe ASPM L1 link power state on the GPU root port (pcie_aspm_rp1_gpu=L1). The capture contains 15 stall bursts, each exactly 12 frames of 21-23 ms (~0.25 s), starting at t=2.40, 6.40, 10.40 ... 58.40 s, i.e. every 4.0 s. Those 15 windows line up 1:1 with the 15 samples where the sensor log reports gpu_pcie_link_state=L1 (seconds 2, 6, 10, ... 58); in every other second the link is L0. MsUntilRenderComplete stays at ~5 ms and MsInPresentAPI at ~0.3 ms during the stalls, so neither CPU nor GPU work grew: the extra ~15 ms per frame is PCIe link exit latency from the L1 low-power state, which the display path then charges to MsBetweenPresents. Nothing else correlates: the Defender burst (seconds 43-45, MsMpEng.exe, disk 80-94%, DPC 396-455 us) and the disk spikes at seconds 13, 27, 52 produced no frame above 7.8 ms, no frames were dropped, SyncInterval=0 (vsync off) so the stalls are not vblank waits, and the GPU link stayed Gen5 x4 with clocks steady at ~2.7 GHz, so the fixed link width is not the trigger. 180 of 8238 frames (2.2%) are stalled, which barely moves the mean but sets the p99, hence normal average FPS with poor 1% lows.",
  "changes": [
    {
      "setting": "pcie_aspm_rp1_gpu",
      "from": "L1",
      "to": "disabled"
    }
  ],
  "notes": {
    "measurement": "avg_fps = 1000 / mean(MsBetweenPresents) = 1000 / 7.284 ms over 8238 frames in 60.0 s; low_1pct_fps = 1000 / p99(MsBetweenPresents) = 1000 / 22.05 ms, per the owner's stated method.",
    "expected_after_fix": "Excluding the 15 ASPM stall bursts, mean frame time is 6.955 ms and p99 is 7.66 ms, i.e. ~143.8 avg FPS with ~130.6 FPS 1% lows. Removing the L1 stalls recovers the 1% lows; this is a calculation from the capture, not a re-measurement.",
    "constraints_respected": "gpu_link_speed Gen5 and gpu_link_width x4 are untouched, and no BIOS overclock setting (xmp_profile, cpu_pbo, cpu_core_ratio) is changed. ASPM is a link power-management setting, not an overclock, so disabling it on the GPU root port stays inside the constraints.",
    "unchanged_despite_being_suspicious": "pcie_aspm_rp0_nvme=L1, power_plan=Balanced, defender (scan at 21:00 plus MsMpEng activity in the capture) and the disk spikes have no timing correlation with any stalled frame, so they are left alone; only the setting proven to cause the stalls is changed.",
    "assumptions": "The two capture files share a clock as the owner states, so sensor second N covers PresentMon times N.0-N.999. The 4.0 s period is the platform's ASPM entry timer, not something the game controls."
  }
}
